he mutation in this detached tree. Found by both\n      reviewers of its second review round by mutation of the removal line; the last round leaves it to the registry.\n    risk_level: low\n    follow_ups: >\n      In `relecture-mutation.test.ts`, assert after the round that `git worktree list` names only the branch's tree and\n      that the detached tree's path no longer exists; the mutation removing `retirerArbre` must make it fail.\n    status: open\n  - bug_id: BUG-2026-10-10T230000\n    date: \"2026-10-10\"\n    title: \"A reference campaign that fails for a passing cause can only be replayed by sending the story back to the red-green\"\n    severity: low\n    priority: p3\n    scope: cycle\n    what_happened: >\n      The tool plays the reference campaigns in the acceptance step (`jouerCampagnes`, `cycle/src/cycle.ts`) only\n      when no acceptance run is prepared since the last reopening: once the acceptance session has recorded\n      `preparee`, `pasRecette` returns the owner's question before reaching the campaigns. A campaign that fails for a\n      cause foreign to the branch — the network while its target installs, the model's API — or a head moved after the\n      campaigns ran therefore leaves the agreement refused (`campagneEnCause`, `cycle/src/campagnes-exigees.ts`) with no\n      way to play the campaigns again but `cycle <story> ecart`, which reopens the story to the red-green and runs the\n      review and the acceptance session again. In an unattended run the story stops at the refused arbitration.\n    what_expected: >\n      The owner, or the unattended run, can have the tool play the reference campaigns again at the current head\n      without reopening the story, the agreement still refused until both are green at the revision it accepts.\n    steps_to_reproduce:\n      - \"On a branch that changes a file under `src/adapters/execution/`, run the acceptance step with a campaign command that fails for `maven`.\"\n      - \"Run `cycle <story> accepte`: refused, naming the maven campaign.\"\n      - \"Run `cycle <story>` again: the step answers the prepared question and plays no campaign; only `cycle <story> ecart` leads to a new play.\"\n    root_cause: >\n      `pasRecette` keys the whole acceptance step on the `preparee` event, and the campaigns were placed before the\n      acceptance session within that step; nothing reads a refused or outdated campaign as a reason to play them again.\n    evidence: >\n      Read in `pasRecette` and `jouerCampagnes` (`cycle/src/cycle.ts`) during the self-review of the branch that makes\n      the tool play the campaigns; not run against a real failing campaign.\n    risk_level: low\n    follow_ups: >\n      Decide whether a refused agreement replays the campaigns at the head on the next run of the step, or whether a\n      command of the owner asks for it; either is a new mechanism of the acceptance step, with its own test.\n    status: open\nb2ec464e docs: the registry records that a reference campaign failed for a passing cause can only be replayed by reopening the story\n77cc7543 feat: before the first review round the cycle mutates the TypeScript source lines the branch introduces with the tests the tasks name, in a detached tree, keeps the report in the journal and names each surviving mutant in the reviewers' prompt, or says why the mutation did not complete or that no line was to be mutated\nb696816a feat: a bypass of a story's security guarantee found in review holds the gate whatever its location or category, is replayed until closed, and goes to the owner instead of the registry\n10c165c6 feat: an adopted formal TLA+ package is qualified and frozen with the controls, and G5 keeps a program requirement only on its exploration plus passing correspondence cases on the candidate\n496ecdb4 feat: the profile declares a mission for each required review and an acceptance recipe frozen at G2, run by the control runner on the exact candidate, and G5 accepts only on 